<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-READY-M6>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-READY-M6" ;
  triage:title "GET /v1/diagnostics advertises a 5000-row cap but storage silently clamps to 1000 with no cursor or truncation signal" ;
  triage:description "arch-ctm (01M1S6VD1Y1G7CK9WKKA42DVKM) and fenix-C (01M1S751VVM0K4C7ZW6YDPC7BQ, their F2) independently converged (duplicate noted as O2 in fenix-C's report, counted once here); quality-mgr confirmed the storage-side clamp directly: crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs:91 `let limit = query.limit.unwrap_or(100).min(1_000) as i64;` while crates/atm-http-runtime/src/diagnostics_route.rs advertises/accepts up to 5000. No cursor/next_cursor, no route-specific read-concurrency or deadline bound, so a 20k-row retained timeline is neither fully traversable nor explicitly admission-bounded. Fix: single shared const for the cap (align route and storage), documented effective cap, stable opaque cursor + next_cursor, indexed query-plan test, semaphore/timeout/load-shed on reads." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "api-contract" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T16:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
